      <div>
        <span class="eyebrow reveal"><svg class="iris-mark" viewBox="0 0 24 24" aria-hidden="true" focusable="false" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.2"><circle cx="12" cy="12" r="10"/><circle cx="12" cy="12" r="5.2"/><circle cx="12" cy="12" r="1.8" fill="currentColor" stroke="none"/></svg>The name</span>
        <h2 class="h2 reveal" data-d="1" style="margin-top:18px">AYiN means <span class="italic-accent">the eye.</span></h2>
        <p class="reveal" data-d="2">In the languages of the ancient Near East, <span class="lead-word">ayin</span> is the eye - perception, insight, the faculty of seeing what others miss. It is the right name for what we do.</p>
        <p class="reveal" data-d="3">Entering the United States is rarely defeated by a weak product. It is defeated by misreading the market - the regional nuance, the buying culture, the partner who looks right but isn't. In our B2B Partnerships practice, which serves the US, Canada and Latin America, we are the eye that reads it clearly, before you commit.</p>
        <p class="reveal" data-d="4">The same habit runs through our AI Solutions Development and Digital Presence practices: understand the situation first, then do the work.</p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </div>
