      <div class="left">
        <span class="eyebrow reveal"><svg class="iris-mark" viewBox="0 0 24 24" aria-hidden="true" focusable="false" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.2"><circle cx="12" cy="12" r="10"/><circle cx="12" cy="12" r="5.2"/><circle cx="12" cy="12" r="1.8" fill="currentColor" stroke="none"/></svg>How we work</span>
        <h2 class="h2 reveal" data-d="1">Principles that hold<br />on the ground.</h2>
      </div>
      <p class="muted reveal" data-d="2" style="max-width:34ch">We keep engagements small and accountable - measured by results, not slides. In partnerships, that means partners signed.</p>
    </div>
    <div class="approach-grid">
      <div class="ap reveal"><div class="k">i.</div><h3 class="h3">Built to be used</h3><p>We deliver what you can put to work - the route to market, the application, the website - not a deck that sits on a shelf.</p></div>
      <div class="ap reveal" data-d="1"><div class="k">ii.</div><h3 class="h3">Founder-aligned</h3><p>Candid counsel from the founder, with incentives tied to traction. You work with the founder, every meeting.</p></div>
      <div class="ap reveal" data-d="2"><div class="k">iii.</div><h3 class="h3">Evidence over theory</h3><p>Every recommendation is grounded in evidence, not assumption. In partnerships, that means real demand signals and real conversations with the market.</p></div>
      <div class="ap reveal"><div class="k">iv.</div><h3 class="h3">Warm, not cold</h3><p>In partnerships, we open doors through relationships we already hold. Introductions arrive with trust attached, so they convert.</p></div>
      <div class="ap reveal" data-d="1"><div class="k">v.</div><h3 class="h3">Sequenced, not open-ended</h3><p>Clear phases with defined outcomes. You always know what comes next and what it costs - no drifting retainers.</p></div>
      <div class="ap reveal" data-d="2"><div class="k">vi.</div><h3 class="h3">Built to hand over</h3><p>Success is your team running the engine without us. We hand over what we built - in partnerships, the relationships and the playbook - then step back.</p></div>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>

